# TRAINING FIXTURE for linux-hardening-001 (hardening capstone lab).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file is a deliberately planted WEAKNESS for students to find and fix
# during the lab. One entry below calls a script from a world-writable
# directory — a classic persistence weakness (CIS benchmark territory): any
# local user could replace that script and it would run every minute.
# Nothing here is executed by the lab environment; it exists so the
# posture-check has something real to flag and the student has something
# real to remediate.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Student's legitimate jobs:
0 2 * * * student /usr/bin/find ~/backups -type f -mtime +30 -delete
*/15 * * * * student /home/student/bin/health-check.sh

# --- planted weakness: script lives in a world-writable directory ---
* * * * * student /tmp/sync.sh
